      "local_deviation": "Local project settings may configure bounded workspace and sandbox resources, but secrets and arbitrary host paths must remain outside renderer state and outside the page contract.",
      "judgment_rationale": "The production Web Project Settings page updates or deletes project metadata, reads the sandbox and its stats, and exposes restart and terminate controls. Sandbox reads are project-member safe, update, restart and terminate require project admin or owner authority, and delete remains project-owner only. Ensure, health, sync, execute, terminal, desktop and proxy-cookie endpoints are not called by this routed page and belong to a wider sandbox capability instead. Desktop now binds the production user_id identity contract and revision-bound project scope, so its controller loads the project, sandbox and sandbox-stats records. ProjectAdministrationPage renders only the project record and exposes none of the update, delete, sandbox inspection, restart or terminate interactions, so client-only mutation methods are excluded from the Desktop Cloud API projection. The latent typed update method still sends PATCH while the production project route accepts PUT; this remains an explicit completion gap while Cloud stays partial with view only. Local binds the same real route but remains renderer-declared and closed with local_project_settings_authority_unavailable."
